Common Issues and Solutions
Issue 1: SSH Connection Refused
Problem: Cannot connect to managed nodes via SSH Solution:

# Check if SSH service is running on target hosts
ansible all -m shell -a "systemctl status sshd" --ask-pass

# Verify SSH key permissions
ls -la ~/.ssh/ansible_key*
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/ansible_key
Issue 2: Permission Denied (publickey)
Problem: SSH key authentication fails Solution:

# Verify public key is in authorized_keys
ssh ansible@192.168.1.10 "cat ~/.ssh/authorized_keys"

# Re-copy public key if needed
ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/ansible_key.pub ansible@192.168.1.10
Issue 3: Inventory Parsing Errors
Problem: Ansible cannot parse inventory file Solution:

# Validate YAML syntax
python3 -c "import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('inventories/webservers.yml'))"

# Check for common YAML issues (indentation, special characters)
ansible-inventory -i inventories/webservers.yml --list
